.TH "DIFFT" "1" "" "difftastic" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
\f[B]difft\f[R] \- a structural diff tool that understands syntax
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]difft\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]OLD\-PATH\f[R]
\f[I]NEW\-PATH\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]DIRECTORY\-ONE\f[R]
\f[I]DIRECTORY\-TWO\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]FILE\-WITH\-CONFLICTS\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]DISPLAY\-PATH\f[R]
\f[I]OLD\-FILE\f[R] \f[I]OLD\-HEX\f[R] \f[I]OLD\-MODE\f[R]
\f[I]NEW\-FILE\f[R] \f[I]NEW\-HEX\f[R] \f[I]NEW\-MODE\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]] \f[I]OLD\-NAME\f[R]
\f[I]OLD\-FILE\f[R] \f[I]OLD\-HEX\f[R] \f[I]OLD\-MODE\f[R]
\f[I]NEW\-FILE\f[R] \f[I]NEW\-HEX\f[R] \f[I]NEW\-MODE\f[R]
\f[I]NEW\-NAME\f[R] \f[I]METADATA\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] \f[B]\-\-list\-languages\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] \f[B]\-\-help\f[R]
.PP
\f[B]difft\f[R] \f[B]\-\-version\f[R]
.SH DESCRIPTION
difftastic (difft) is a CLI diff tool that compares files based on their
syntax, not line\-by\-line.
Difftastic produces accurate diffs that are easier for humans to read.
.PP
Difftastic normally compares two paths.
If both paths are directories, difftastic walks them recursively and
compares files with matching names.
A path of \f[B]\-\f[R] reads that file from standard input, and
\f[B]/dev/null\f[R] is treated as an empty file.
.PP
If a single path is given, difftastic looks for \f[B]<<<<<<<\f[R]
conflict markers in that file, reconstructs the two conflicting file
states, and diffs those.
.PP
The 7 and 9 argument forms are the calling conventions used by
\f[B]GIT_EXTERNAL_DIFF\f[R], so difftastic can be invoked directly by
git.
See the manual for how to configure git, Mercurial, Jujutsu or Fossil to
use difftastic.
.SS OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-background\f[R] \f[I]BACKGROUND\f[R]
Set the background brightness.
Difftastic will prefer brighter colours on dark backgrounds.
.RS
.PP
Possible values: \f[I]dark\f[R], \f[I]light\f[R].
Default: \f[I]dark\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_BACKGROUND\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-byte\-limit\f[R] \f[I]LIMIT\f[R]
Use a line\-oriented diff if either input file exceeds this size.
.RS
.PP
Default: \f[I]1000000\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_BYTE_LIMIT\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-check\-only\f[R]
Report whether there are any changes, but don\[cq]t calculate them.
Much faster.
.RS
.PP
Difftastic does not parse the files in this mode, so any byte difference
is reported as a change.
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_CHECK_ONLY\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-color\f[R] \f[I]WHEN\f[R]
When to use color output.
.RS
.PP
Possible values: \f[I]always\f[R], \f[I]auto\f[R], \f[I]never\f[R].
Default: \f[I]auto\f[R], which uses colour when the output is a terminal
or when the git pager is in use.
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_COLOR\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-context\f[R] \f[I]LINES\f[R]
The number of contextual lines to show around changed lines.
.RS
.PP
Default: \f[I]3\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_CONTEXT\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-display\f[R] \f[I]MODE\f[R]
Display mode for showing results.
.RS
.PP
\f[I]side\-by\-side\f[R]: Display the before file and the after file in
two separate columns, with line numbers aligned according to unchanged
content.
If a change is exclusively additions or exclusively removals, use a
single column.
.PP
\f[I]side\-by\-side\-show\-both\f[R]: The same as
\f[I]side\-by\-side\f[R], but always uses two columns.
.PP
\f[I]inline\f[R]: A single column display, closer to traditional diff
display.
.PP
\f[I]json\f[R]: Output the results as a machine\-readable JSON array
with an element per file.
This is an unstable feature whose format may change, so it also requires
the environment variable \f[B]DFT_UNSTABLE\f[R] to be set.
.PP
Default: \f[I]side\-by\-side\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_DISPLAY\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-exit\-code\f[R]
Set the exit code to 1 if there are syntactic changes in any files.
For files where there is no detected language (e.g.\ unsupported
language or binary files), sets the exit code if there are any byte
changes.
.RS
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_EXIT_CODE\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-graph\-limit\f[R] \f[I]LIMIT\f[R]
Use a line\-oriented diff if the internal graph exceeds this number of
vertices.
This limit controls the worst case runtime and memory usage for
difftastic.
.RS
.PP
Higher values will allow difftastic to perform a structural diff in more
cases.
Higher values will also increase the time before difftastic gives up on
structural diffing, and increase peak memory usage.
.PP
Default: \f[I]3000000\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_GRAPH_LIMIT\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-h, \-\-help\f[R]
Print help information.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-ignore\-comments\f[R]
Don\[cq]t consider comments when diffing.
.RS
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_IGNORE_COMMENTS\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-list\-languages\f[R]
Print all the languages supported by difftastic, along with their
recognised extensions.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-override\f[R] \f[I]GLOB:NAME\f[R]
Associate this glob pattern with this language, overriding normal
language detection.
For example:
.RS
.IP
.EX
$ difft \-\-override=\[aq]*.c:C++\[aq] old.c new.c
.EE
.PP
See \f[B]\-\-list\-languages\f[R] for the list of language names.
Language names are matched case insensitively.
Overrides may also specify the language \f[I]\[lq]text\[rq]\f[R] to
treat a file as plain text.
.PP
This argument may be given more than once.
For example:
.IP
.EX
$ difft \-\-override=\[aq]CustomFile:json\[aq] \-\-override=\[aq]*.c:text\[aq] old.c new.c
.EE
.PP
To configure multiple overrides using environment variables, difftastic
also accepts \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_1\f[R] up to \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_9\f[R].
.IP
.EX
$ export DFT_OVERRIDE=\[aq]CustomFile:json\[aq]
$ export DFT_OVERRIDE_1=\[aq]*.c:text\[aq]
$ export DFT_OVERRIDE_2=\[aq]*.js:javascript jsx\[aq]
.EE
.PP
When multiple overrides are specified, the first matching override wins.
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-override\-binary\f[R] \f[I]GLOB\f[R]
Always treat file names matching this glob as binary files, ignoring the
default heuristics for binary detection.
For example:
.RS
.IP
.EX
$ difft \-\-override\-binary=\[aq]*.gz\[aq] old.gz new.gz
.EE
.PP
This argument may be given more than once.
For example:
.IP
.EX
$ difft \-\-override\-binary=\[aq]*.gz\[aq] \-\-override\-binary=\[aq]foo.pickle\[aq] old.gz new.gz
.EE
.PP
To configure multiple overrides using environment variables, difftastic
also accepts \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY_1\f[R] up to
\f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY_9\f[R].
.IP
.EX
$ export DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY=\[aq]*.gz\[aq]
$ export DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY_1=\[aq]*.bz2\[aq]
$ export DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY_2=\[aq]foo.pickle\[aq]
.EE
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-parse\-error\-limit\f[R] \f[I]LIMIT\f[R]
Use a line\-oriented diff if the number of parse errors exceeds this
value.
.RS
.PP
A value of 0 means that any parse error will make difftastic use a
line\-oriented diff.
.PP
Default: \f[I]0\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_PARSE_ERROR_LIMIT\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-skip\-unchanged\f[R]
Don\[cq]t display anything if a file is unchanged.
This is useful when comparing directories of files.
.RS
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_SKIP_UNCHANGED\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-sort\-paths\f[R]
When diffing a directory, output the results sorted by path.
This is slower.
.RS
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_SORT_PATHS\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-strip\-cr\f[R] \f[I]on/off\f[R]
Remove any carriage return characters before diffing.
This can be helpful when dealing with files on Windows that contain CRLF
line endings.
.RS
.PP
When disabled, difftastic will consider multiline string literals (in
code) or multiline text (e.g.\ in HTML) to differ if the two input files
have different line endings.
.PP
Possible values: \f[I]on\f[R], \f[I]off\f[R].
Default: \f[I]on\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_STRIP_CR\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-syntax\-highlight\f[R] \f[I]on/off\f[R]
Enable or disable syntax highlighting.
.RS
.PP
Possible values: \f[I]on\f[R], \f[I]off\f[R].
Default: \f[I]on\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_SYNTAX_HIGHLIGHT\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-\-tab\-width\f[R] \f[I]NUM_SPACES\f[R]
Treat a tab as this many spaces.
.RS
.PP
Default: \f[I]4\f[R].
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_TAB_WIDTH\f[R].
.RE
.TP
\f[B]\-V, \-\-version\f[R]
Print version information.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-width\f[R] \f[I]COLUMNS\f[R]
Use this many columns when calculating line wrapping.
If not specified, difftastic will detect the terminal width.
.RS
.PP
Environment variable: \f[B]DFT_WIDTH\f[R].
.RE
.SS DEBUG OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dump\-syntax\f[R] \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Parse a single file with tree\-sitter and display the difftastic syntax
tree.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dump\-syntax\-dot\f[R] \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Parse a single file with tree\-sitter and display the difftastic syntax
tree, as a DOT graph.
.TP
\f[B]\-\-dump\-ts\f[R] \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Parse a single file with tree\-sitter and display the tree\-sitter parse
tree.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
Every difftastic option can also be set with an environment variable,
which is useful when a version control tool invokes \f[B]difft\f[R]
directly.
The variable for each option is listed in OPTIONS above.
For example, \f[B]DFT_BACKGROUND=light\f[R] is equivalent to
\f[B]\-\-background=light\f[R].
.PP
Command line arguments take precedence over the corresponding
environment variable.
.TP
\f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_1\f[R] to \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_9\f[R]
Additional language overrides, in the same \f[I]GLOB:NAME\f[R] format as
\f[B]\-\-override\f[R].
Unlike \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE\f[R], these are always applied, even when
\f[B]\-\-override\f[R] is also given.
.TP
\f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY_1\f[R] to \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY_9\f[R]
Additional binary file globs, in the same format as
\f[B]\-\-override\-binary\f[R].
Unlike \f[B]DFT_OVERRIDE_BINARY\f[R], these are always applied, even
when \f[B]\-\-override\-binary\f[R] is also given.
.TP
\f[B]DFT_UNSTABLE\f[R]
Enable unstable features whose behaviour may change in future releases.
This is currently required by \f[B]\-\-display=json\f[R].
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
\f[B]0\f[R]
Difftastic ran successfully.
Without \f[B]\-\-exit\-code\f[R], this is also returned when difftastic
finds changes.
.TP
\f[B]1\f[R]
Difftastic was run with \f[B]\-\-exit\-code\f[R] and found syntactic
changes in a text file, or byte changes in a binary file.
.TP
\f[B]2\f[R]
Difftastic was given invalid arguments.
This includes invalid usage (e.g.\ the wrong number of arguments) as
well as paths that difftastic cannot read (e.g.\ non\-existent paths or
insufficient permissions).
.SH EXAMPLES
Compare two files.
.IP
.EX
$ difft old.js new.js
.EE
.PP
Compare two directories.
.IP
.EX
$ difft old/ new/
.EE
.PP
Compare a file against a previous version read from standard input.
.IP
.EX
$ git show HEAD:foo.js | difft \- foo.js
.EE
.PP
Diff a file that still contains conflict markers.
.IP
.EX
$ difft file_with_conflicts.js
.EE
.PP
Use difftastic for a single git command.
.IP
.EX
$ git \-c diff.external=difft diff
.EE
